> [Level] 2 NVQ[ Di]ploma in Wood Occupations (Timber Frame Erection) - Q2W Ltd.
The Level 2 NVQ[ Di]ploma in Wood Occupations – Timber Frame Erection is designed to assess occupational competence in the workplace. Learners are required to demonstrate their skills, knowledge and experience in the construction of timber frame buildings. This qualification is suitable for practicing timber frame carpenters.
This NVQ provides formal recognition of practicing as timber frame carpenter.
There are no formal entry requirements for this NVQ qualification, however the potential learner must be able to demonstrate[ that] they can meet the skills, knowledge and experience requirements of the NVQ in timber frame carpentry[ before] enrolment[.]
The Level 2 NVQ[ Di]ploma in Wood Occupations – Timber Frame Erection qualifies the holder to apply[ for the] Construction Skills Certification Scheme (CSCS)[ blue] skill card ([https]://www.csc[s].uk.com/[card]-type/manager/).[]

