> The OTR 1840 is a CWDM Fiber Optic to SDI transmitter and receiver[ combined] in[ a] compact self contained package. It is a convenient and cost effective solution to combat the restrictions involved with the distribution of uncompressed broadcast quality video signals over long distances.
Each OTR 1840 CWDM tranceiver[ has] an independ[ant] transmitter[ and] receiver[ channel,] which provides an effective solution for any SDI signal up to 1080[p]60[ (]3[G]bit/s) while preserving full uncompressed quality. Select from 18 transmitter wavelengths for full CWDM compatibility[ (]ITU-T[ G].694.2).
The OTR 1840 will auto-detect[ and re]-clock any 270Mbit[ /] 1.5[G]bit[ and] 3[Gbit] SDI source[ prior] to[ conversion].[ The] module is fully compatible with 3[G]bit Level A[ and Level] B formats[.]

